It includes the following third-party data:

Turbo colormap (include/holoscan/mono_depth/colormap.hpp)
Copyright 2019 Google LLC. Designed by Anton Mikhailov.
Licensed under Apache-2.0
(https://gist.github.com/mikhailov-work/ee72ba4191942acecc03fe6da94fc73f). Its
published 256-entry table, rounded to 8 bits per channel.

The models are NOT part of holoscan-mono-depth. tools/prepare_model.py (installed as
share/holoscan-mono-depth/prepare_model.py) downloads a pinned checkpoint from Hugging
Face, checks its SHA-256 digest, and exports it with a separately installed PyTorch
and Hugging Face Transformers. The checkpoints and their licenses:

- small (the default): depth-anything/Depth-Anything-V2-Small-hf, revision
  5426e4f0f36572d16453bbda7a8389317b1bef99. Licensed under Apache-2.0 by its
  authors (the model card's license, and the Depth Anything V2 repository's
  "Depth-Anything-V2-Small model is under the Apache-2.0 license").
- base and large: depth-anything/Depth-Anything-V2-Base-hf (revision
  b1958afc87fb45a9e3746cb387596094de553ed8) and Depth-Anything-V2-Large-hf
  (revision 7581137eff8d4e94f6e796d3baea0e9fa79b22d2). Licensed under CC-BY-NC-4.0:
  NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY. The tool exports them only with
  --accept-non-commercial-license.
- metric-indoor-small and metric-outdoor-small:
  depth-anything/Depth-Anything-V2-Metric-Indoor-Small-hf (revision
  8078d68a9c75a972131914f6afd0c1723be0da7f) and
  depth-anything/Depth-Anything-V2-Metric-Outdoor-Small-hf (revision
  fd2c22027eaf20374204f14099b8341e1925ad39), fine-tuned on Hypersim and Virtual
  KITTI 2. These Transformers conversions carry no license tag; the same authors
  publish the original checkpoints (Depth-Anything-V2-Metric-Hypersim-Small and
  Depth-Anything-V2-Metric-VKITTI-Small) under Apache-2.0.

Depth Anything V2: Lihe Yang, Bingyi Kang, Zilong Huang, Zhen Zhao, Xiaogang Xu,
